course: dictionary
lesson: 2645
title: Detectors and what they find
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A detector is a machine or device that notices or finds something. A smoke detector notices smoke and warns us of fire. A metal detector finds metal. Detectors help us find things we could not notice alone.
explain: Context helps you here too. «A metal detector at the end of a food line throws out any packet with even a tiny bit of metal.» The words «throws out» and «packet» tell you the detector finds something, and then it acts on what it finds.
explain: Some detectors find things we cannot see or hear. «Most bat calls are ultrasound, too high for grown-ups to hear; a bat detector turns them into clicks we can hear.» The detector changes a sound we cannot hear into one we can.
fact: A detector is a machine or device that notices or finds something.
fact: Smoke detectors, also called smoke alarms, warn us of fire, so test them regularly.
fact: Metal detectors are used at airports and in food factories to find metal.
fact: Scientists use detectors to measure things like light or heat.
fact: A detector can help us hear sounds that are too high for our ears, such as bat calls.
exercise: «A metal detector at the end of a food line throws out any packet with even a tiny bit of metal.» What does the metal detector do? | *Finds packets that have metal in them | Counts the children in the line | Makes the food cold | Weighs each packet
exercise: «A bat detector turns them into clicks we can hear.» What does a bat detector do? | *Turns sounds too high for us into clicks we can hear | Catches bats in a net | Turns off the lights | Makes bats fly faster
exercise: «Most bat calls are ultrasound, too high for grown-ups to hear; a bat detector turns them into clicks we can hear.» Find and copy the word that means sounds too high for us to hear. | grown-ups | *ultrasound | bat | clicks
test: «A hammerhead's wide head sweeps the sand like a metal detector for hidden stingrays.» Why does the hammerhead sweep the sand like a metal detector? | *To find hidden stingrays | To dig a hole to sleep in | To make the sand wet | To swim backwards
test: Which device warns us of fire? | A cup of tea | *A smoke detector | A bowl of porcelain | A kite
exam: Which device checks people for metal at an airport? | Smoke detector | Lie detector | *Metal detector | Motion sensor light
